Below is a compact representation of every **client‑side FTP request** (the commands a client can send to an FTP server).  
Each entry is shown as a **template string** that a client would send – i.e. the command name plus any required argument(s) – terminated with `\r\n` exactly as it appears on the wire.

```json
{
  "FTP": [
    "USER <<username>>\r\n",
    "PASS <<password>>\r\n",
    "ACCT <<account>>\r\n",
    "CWD <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "CDUP\r\n",
    "QUIT\r\n",
    "REIN\r\n",
    "PORT <<host-port>>\r\n",
    "PASV\r\n",
    "TYPE <<type>>\r\n",
    "STRU <<structure>>\r\n",
    "MODE <<mode>>\r\n",
    "RETR <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "STOR <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "STOU <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "APPE <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "ALLO <<size>>\r\n",
    "REST <<marker>>\r\n",
    "RNFR <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "RNTO <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "ABOR\r\n",
    "DELE <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "RMD <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "MKD <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "PWD\r\n",
    "LIST <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "NLST <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "SITE <<string>>\r\n",
    "SYST\r\n",
    "STAT <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "HELP <<command>>\r\n",
    "NOOP\r\n"
  ]
}
```

### What the placeholders mean
| Placeholder | Meaning (RFC 959) |
|-------------|-------------------|
| `<<username>>` | User identifier for the session. |
| `<<password>>` | Password for the user (sent in clear‑text on a plain FTP connection). |
| `<<account>>` | Account information (optional, used with `ACCT`). |
| `<<pathname>>` | A file or directory name (relative or absolute). |
| `<<host-port>>` | 32‑bit IP‑
Below are additional FTP client request templates, including **extended/additional commands** that are commonly used beyond the core RFC 959 set:

```json
{
  "FTP_EXTENDED": [
    "FEAT\r\n",
    "OPTS <<option>> <<value>>\r\n",
    "PBSZ <<size>>\r\n",
    "PROT <<level>>\r\n",
    "EPRT <<extended-host-port>>\r\n",
    "EPSV\r\n",
    "EPSV <<mode>>\r\n",
    "MDTM <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "SIZE <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "MLST <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "MLSD <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "AUTH <<auth-type>>\r\n",
    "ADAT <<base64-data>>\r\n",
    "CCC\r\n",
    "MIC <<base64-command>>\r\n",
    "CONF <<base64-command>>\r\n",
    "ENC <<base64-command>>\r\n",
    "SMNT <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "XCUP\r\n",
    "XPWD\r\n",
    "XMKD <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "XRMD <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "XCWD <<pathname>>\r\n",
    "XATM <<datetime>> <<pathname>>\r\n"
  ]
}
```

### Extended Commands Reference

| Command | Description | RFC |
|---------|-------------|-----|
| `FEAT` | List protocol features server supports | 2389 |
| `OPTS` | Set options for a command | 2389 |
| `PBSZ` | Protection Buffer Size | 2228 |
| `PROT` | Data channel protection level | 2228 |
| `EPRT` | Extended PORT (IPv6 support) | 2428 |
| `EPSV` | Extended PASV (IPv6 support) | 2428 |
| `MDTM` | File modification time | 3659 |
| `SIZE` | File size | 3659 |
| `MLST/MLSD` | Machine-readable directory listing | 3659 |
| `AUTH` | Authentication mechanism | 2228 |
| `XCUP/XCWD/etc.` | Compatibility aliases (Unix-style) | — |